{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition","id":1432523,"title":"[2ed CofD/WtF] Guide for creating new homebrew shapeshifters/changers for 2 edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-17T11:20:54-08:00","id":1432523,"title":"[2ed CofD/WtF] Guide for creating new homebrew shapeshifters/changers for 2 edition","content":"Hi how are yall? I wanted to know if there was a guide of or atleas some ruleset or something that guide you in creating a new species of shapeshifters/shapechangers for second edition<br /> <br /> I know shapechangers and skinchangers (and also changing breeds) existed for frist edition but i dont know any guide or anything for 2 edition that helps you in regards on how to make/add new shapeshifters <br /> <br /> And i would be interested if anyone know of homebrews that add that into 2ed cofd <br /> <br /> And sorry if i did something wron and for the bad gramma its my frist time making a topic here \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26408-luchya","name":"Luchya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T11:36:02-08:00","id":1432524,"title":"","content":"Skinchangers got a quick 2E update in the form of a Merit in the Under the Skin era of the first Dark Eras book. It's nowhere near as extensive as a full supplement, but it's something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T12:00:55-08:00","id":1432526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition?p=1432524#post1432524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skinchangers got a quick 2E update in the form of a Merit in the Under the Skin era of the first Dark Eras book. It's nowhere near as extensive as a full supplement, but it's something.</div> </div> </div> </div>But nothing in the lines of making new shapeshifters like the urathra for 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26408-luchya","user":"Luchya","date":". 01-17-2021, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26408-luchya","name":"Luchya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T12:10:08-08:00","id":1432528,"title":"","content":"Acrozatarim, one of the writer developers for Werewolf in second edition, had a write-up about the Bull-Headed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1328351-bull-headed-2e-rules-for-the-gudthabak-bull-shifters\">here</a>. And Dark Eras 2's Ancient Egypt chapter has a write-up about the Sobeki crocodile-shifters.<br /> <br /> But there is no 'Make Uratha, but another animal' guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T12:49:54-08:00","id":1432532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition?p=1432528#post1432528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acrozatarim, one of the writer developers for Werewolf in second edition, had a write-up about the Bull-Headed <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1328351-bull-headed-2e-rules-for-the-gudthabak-bull-shifters&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. And Dark Eras 2's Ancient Egypt chapter has a write-up about the Sobeki crocodile-shifters.<br /> <br /> But there is no 'Make Uratha, but another animal' guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could it maybe be possible to create other shapeshifters with out guide then \ud83d\ude05 (following some rulesets of 2ed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26408-luchya","name":"Luchya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T13:26:57-08:00","id":1432535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luchya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition?p=1432532#post1432532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could it maybe be possible to create other shapeshifters with out guide then \ud83d\ude05 (following some rulesets of 2ed)</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, just a matter of what the creator wants out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T16:02:46-08:00","id":1432550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition?p=1432528#post1432528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acrozatarim, one of the writer developers for Werewolf in second edition, had a write-up about the Bull-Headed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1328351-bull-headed-2e-rules-for-the-gudthabak-bull-shifters\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not aware of that update. Thanks for bringing it up.<br /> <br /> Also, as someone who has designed a shapeshifter once and made a lot of &quot;variant templates&quot; through the years, my recomendation is to take the closest existing relative (in this case, werewolf, but also Claimed or some other template could work), follow through the whole template's structure and note what of it makes sense for the new template, what needs to be changed and what needs to be outright removed. Than you should think about what makes that new template unique and interesting, and add things accordingly. Sure, it is not na guide as much of a guidline, but I think that if you have a solid concept for your new template, a lot of it will work on its own by using some other existing template as a reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T18:25:24-08:00","id":1432643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition?p=1432528#post1432528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acrozatarim, one of the writer developers for Werewolf in second edition, had a write-up about the Bull-Headed <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1328351-bull-headed-2e-rules-for-the-gudthabak-bull-shifters&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not clear to me whether they\u2019re supposed to have Gifts and Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T18:36:26-08:00","id":1432645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition?p=1432643#post1432643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not clear to me whether they\u2019re supposed to have Gifts and Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't, which is why neither are mentioned.<br /> <br /> Gifts and Renown are (except for Geryo) uniquely werewolf. The former reflect the werewolf's predatory nature, the latter awards from Luna (one of their progenitors) for their achievements. The bull-headed, the Sobeki, the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1415558-2e-update-siten-uzu-the-fox-chosen\">Siten Uzu</a>, and the Lyrebirds and Rot Dogs (bird-shifters and another thing from <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim/posts\" target=\"_blank\">Acrozatarim's Patreon</a>) don't have Gifts or Renown, but do have their own abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-18-2021, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T19:06:41-08:00","id":1432647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition?p=1432643#post1432643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not clear to me whether they\u2019re supposed to have Gifts and Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither are listed and neither would make sense. All Gifts and Renowns are designed for werewolves only. Moon and Wolf Gifts are pretty obvious why that is, but to explain Shadow Gifts: They are expressions of the Uratha's own spiritual powers focused through a theme bestowed by a spirit of a specific nature. That's why so many of them focus on werewolf specific stuff like territory, hunting, tracking, etc.<br /> <br /> While some Shadow Gifts would work for the gudthabak, like the Gift of the Elements, but the fact that they're designed for uratha makes them generally a bad fit for any other type of shapeshifter. As such I recommend either skipping Gifts altogether for a set of innate abilities, or design/convert a very limited list of possible Gifts (or equivalent powers; you could even base them on Disciplines or Haunts, etc) for anyone who seeks to design their own shapeshifters. Same thing with Renown.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=1280951#post1280951\">Here's an example of what I mean.</a> I skipped the Renown completely because they didn't make sense for these particular shifters, and simplified the Gifts to work without them. The Gifts available are just a limited set of thematically appropriate Shadow Gifts, which saved a whole lot of work. If I were to put in some effort in making these guys interesting as either PCs or NPCs I'd slap on a few more innate abilities (which could possibly make the Gifts redundant) and maybe a few (mutually exclusive?) Merits relating to the individual forms since the forms are their most interesting aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T04:58:40-08:00","id":1432675,"title":"","content":"If you are looking for more references, the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1414367-new-shapeshifters-lyrebirds-the-orpheans\">Lyrebirds </a>that nofather have mentioned are found here, while my Cernunni could be found in the STV (see my sig). In my case, I have included Shadow Gifts for the weredeer, but that's due to their strange connection to the Uratha, as werewolves can gain their Gifts by hunting them through a Sacred Hunt (so it is there both to given some edge to the weredeer and to give more reasons for the Uratha to hunt them down). I do, however, agree that Gifts and Renown should not be simply given to any shapeshifter, and definitely not in the same way as the Uratha without having a good reason to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T14:14:18-08:00","id":1432717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1432523-2ed-cofd-wtf-guide-for-creating-new-homebrew-shapeshifters-changers-for-2-edition?p=1432675#post1432675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are looking for more references, the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1414367-new-shapeshifters-lyrebirds-the-orpheans\">Lyrebirds </a>that nofather have mentioned are found here, while my Cernunni could be found in the STV (see my sig). In my case, I have included Shadow Gifts for the weredeer, but that's due to their strange connection to the Uratha, as werewolves can gain their Gifts by hunting them through a Sacred Hunt (so it is there both to given some edge to the weredeer and to give more reasons for the Uratha to hunt them down). I do, however, agree that Gifts and Renown should not be simply given to any shapeshifter, and definitely not in the same way as the Uratha without having a good reason to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, thanks, I must have typo'd my search for them because they weren't coming up, nice that the Lyrebirds are on the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}